From: DuDuClaw OS Y6-1 (2026-08-26)
Subject: CMakeLists.txt: prefix the Fcitx5CompilerSettings include with CMAKE_SYSROOT

Real do_configure failure caught cross-compiling against fcitx5's own
exported CMake config: "CMake Error ... include could not find requested
file: /usr/lib/cmake/Fcitx5Utils/Fcitx5CompilerSettings.cmake" -- the file
genuinely exists (confirmed present in fcitx5's staged recipe-sysroot at
that exact relative path), but CMake's `include()` command is a literal
file-path operation, unlike `find_package()` -- it does NOT get redirected
through CMAKE_SYSROOT/CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH the way find_package() calls do.
`FCITX_INSTALL_CMAKECONFIG_DIR` is set to the bare absolute path
"/usr/lib/cmake" inside fcitx5's own generated Fcitx5UtilsConfig.cmake
(correct from THAT project's own build perspective, wrong once consumed
cross-compiled from a different recipe's sysroot). Same root-cause class as
the upstream-adjacent community fcitx5 Yocto layer's own
"0001-Tweak-include-directories-to-care-CMAKE_SYSROOT.patch" (a different
absolute-path-without-sysroot-prefix spot in fcitx5 core itself,
hyyoxhk/meta-fcitx5) -- confirms this is a known, recurring category of gap
in fcitx5's cross-compile story, not a one-off invented here. Prefixing
with ${CMAKE_SYSROOT} is a no-op on a native (non-cross) build (empty
string), matching that same reference patch's safety property.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet submitted to fcitx/fcitx5-chewing]
Signed-off-by: DuDuClaw OS Y6-1

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
     set(CHEWING_TARGET PkgConfig::Chewing)
 endif()
 
-include("${FCITX_INSTALL_CMAKECONFIG_DIR}/Fcitx5Utils/Fcitx5CompilerSettings.cmake")
+include("${CMAKE_SYSROOT}${FCITX_INSTALL_CMAKECONFIG_DIR}/Fcitx5Utils/Fcitx5CompilerSettings.cmake")
 
 add_subdirectory(src)
 add_subdirectory(data)
